<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">18042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Washington has quietly renewed a thirty-day waiver letting Asian buyers keep purchasing sanctioned Russian crude, even as Treasury Secretary Bessent publicly denied any such relief.</s> <s>The International Energy Agency called the Iran war the worst global energy shock in history, and Asian capitals pressed the US to keep the Russian barrels flowing.</s> <s>The architecture of maximum pressure against Moscow and Tehran can't hold at once... one had to bend, and it did.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>France and the United Kingdom will lead forty-nine nations to police the Strait of Hormuz, through which twenty percent of the world's oil passes, after Washington declined to take the command.</s> <s>Military officials meet at Northwood next week to finalise a mission that could last years.</s> <s>It's the first time since the Suez crisis that Europe has anchored security at a Gulf chokepoint without American leadership.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Dengue fever has returned to Khartoum with the million residents Sudan's government urged back before fixing water and waste systems.</s> <s>In North Darfur, measles kills displaced children daily, and a senior Mahamid commander has defected from the Rapid Support Forces to the army.</s> <s>On the third anniversary of the war, the state's reclamation of the capital is becoming an epidemiological catastrophe.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Afghanistan absorbed one hundred and seventy thousand people fleeing the Iran war, thirteen times the number Pakistan received, the International Organization for Migration reported.</s> <s>Kabul has received no formal international support for the intake, and a ceasefire has now reversed the flow, with Iranians crossing back.</s> <s>The poorest neighbours, not the Gulf capitals, are absorbing the human cost of the conflict.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A ceasefire in Lebanon after forty-six days of strikes has Hezbollah claiming victory and Netanyahu facing a coalition revolt for agreeing to it.</s> <s>Lebanese government figures count more than two thousand one hundred dead and one point two million displaced.</s> <s>Beirut has ten days to show it'll disarm Hezbollah, a condition the group has already refused.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>President Zelensky has warned Minsk that joining Russia's war would mean meeting Venezuela's fate, as Ukrainian intelligence detects roads and artillery massing near the Belarusian border.</s> <s>Lukashenko has simultaneously signed a decree conscripting reserve officers for active duty.</s> <s>A second front would force Kyiv to split its forces just as ceasefire diplomacy circulates in Washington.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Hungary has ended Viktor Orbán's sixteen-year rule, with a seventy-nine point five percent turnout delivering Péter Magyar's Tisza party a two-thirds majority.</s> <s>The opposition overcame gerrymandered districts and state-controlled media through the largest civil mobilisation in post-communist Hungary.</s> <s>Magyar has demanded the resignation of eight senior officials and pledged a new office to investigate Fidesz-era corruption.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Vietnam's general secretary To Lam has named China a strategic choice of overarching and long-term significance, the strongest tilt toward Beijing from Hanoi in a generation.</s> <s>Vietnam has hedged between Washington and Beijing for decades, but Trump-era tariffs have made Chinese supply-chain integration newly attractive.</s> <s>Analysts say the four-day visit marks a structural realignment, not a tactical gesture.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>President Tinubu has signed Nigeria's twenty twenty-six budget while extending last year's deadline, leaving Africa's largest economy running two fiscal years at once.</s> <s>Ministries face dual deadlines, with twenty twenty-five capital projects closing at the end of June even as the new cycle begins.</s> <s>It's a quiet admission that the fiscal machinery can't execute a single budget on schedule.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Australia's green export strategy risks producing stranded assets, the Lowy Institute has warned, because Canberra has committed billions in subsidies without binding offtake deals from Japan, Korea, or the European Union.</s> <s>Green hydrogen, green iron, and critical minerals all require long-term purchase contracts before private capital will follow.</s> <s>It's the structural problem of climate industrial policy: supply-side ambition without demand-side anchors.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Three French carriers have bid twenty-four billion euros to absorb SFR, the country's second-largest mobile operator, reducing the market from four players to three.</s> <s>Regulators who blocked similar consolidation in twenty thirteen now back the deal, citing a European shift from protecting consumer prices to building digital champions.</s> <s>The antitrust review runs until mid-May and will test how far Brussels has truly moved.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers at Concordia University in Montreal have found that dense park canopies can trap heat after sundown and radiate it back into the city at night.</s> <s>Tree arrangement, not coverage, determines whether a park cools its neighbourhood, yet most megacity policies specify only how much canopy to plant.</s> <s>For Delhi, Karachi, or Lagos, the design detail decides whether adaptation budgets reduce mortality or not.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A team at the Charité in Berlin has crossed the cell membrane with a nanobody to refold the defective protein that causes cystic fibrosis, a barrier antibodies normally cannot pass.</s> <s>The work, in Nature Chemical Biology, opens a route to other misfolded-protein diseases including Alzheimer's and Parkinson's.</s> <s>It's the kind of basic-science breakthrough that rewrites what therapeutics can reach, in sha'Allah.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Five people have died in Burundi from an unidentified illness that's defied testing.</s> <s>Africa Centres for Disease Control has ruled out Ebola, Marburg, Rift Valley fever, and two other haemorrhagic fevers, and a rapid response team has deployed to Mpanda District.</s> <s>The agency is tracking ninety-two high-risk health events across the continent, a reminder that surveillance capacity is the thin line between outbreak and pandemic.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Fifteen million dollars has been drained from Grinex, the Kyrgyzstan-registered crypto exchange widely seen as the successor to the sanctioned Russian platform Garantex.</s> <s>Grinex had processed more than six billion dollars as Russia's largest ruble-to-crypto rail, and its suspension leaves sanctioned flows without an established platform.</s> <s>The exchange has blamed western special services, making this an operational picture of economic warfare running through chain-level hacks rather than SWIFT notices.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>AI infrastructure built in the United States and Europe is routing its toxic hardware to informal dismantling yards in Ghana, Nigeria, Pakistan, and Vietnam, Rest of World has reported.</s> <s>No law tracks where the servers end up, and data-centre operators bear none of the disposal cost.</s> <s>Workers in Accra and Lagos absorb what the AI boom leaves behind, one broken board at a time.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Apple and Samsung have blocked India's sixth attempt to mandate Aadhaar identity preloading on smartphones, citing security, compatibility, and production costs.</s> <s>Aadhaar links fingerprints and iris scans for one point three four billion residents, and New Delhi has tried six times in two years to force it onto devices at the factory.</s> <s>That two of the world's largest manufacturers keep refusing shows the friction biometric states face when hardware makers hold the line.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>